From 1e9daaca565fa727d8ea7278589e45d787a5768b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:17:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/40] sunxi: h713: take the panel from the identified image,
 not the project ID

Which panel is fitted is a property of the device. The project ID only
selects a TSE group, and nothing stops two boards with different panels
from sharing one -- but because both boards in the revision table happen
to have an ID of their own, choosing the panel by project ID and choosing
it by device gave the same answer, and the shortcut looked correct.

It is not. A third board reporting project 0x34 would be driven with the
bench board's 1280x720 timing because that is what 0x34 means in the
table, whatever panel it actually has.

So select from the row the digest identified, and fall back to the
project ID only when the image is unknown -- saying, when that happens,
that the panel is a guess.

That needs the identity earlier than it was available: h713_disp_lookup()
runs before the release path, where h713_mips_verify() used to be the
first thing to hash the image. Hash it in h713_disp_load() instead, right
after the file is read. Verify runs again before release and is
idempotent; it now also clears any previous load's identity, which it
should always have done.

While moving that around, the two loaders' identical size checks -- one
in h713_mips_load(), one in h713_disp_load(), each with its own message
-- become one h713_mips_accept_size().

No functional change on either known board.
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c | 94 +++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 59 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
index 79d13b4fda4..d49ac835681 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
@@ -386,6 +386,28 @@ static const struct h713_mips_fw_rev *h713_board_by_project(u32 project)
  */
 static ulong h713_mips_fw_size = H713_MIPS_FW_SIZE;
 
+/*
+ * Accept any size a known revision declares; the digest decides which one it
+ * is. Refusing here on one revision's size turns an identity check into a size
+ * check. Both loaders had arrived at the same conclusion separately, in two
+ * copies of the same loop, so they now ask the same question in one place.
+ */
+static int h713_mips_accept_size(ulong len)
+{
+	uint i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(h713_mips_fw_revs); i++) {
+		if (len != h713_mips_fw_revs[i].size)
+			continue;
+		h713_mips_fw_size = len;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	printf("H713 MIPS: rejected size 0x%lx, no revision declares it\n", len);
+
+	return -EINVAL;
+}
+
 /*
